# A script's first runs on each engine, 2026-11-25: `hello`, a 500-line script and cigo

<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0 -->

`cig run --engine vm` lowers a script to bytecode the first time it runs it, and keeps the module in the tin for the runs after. `cig run` on the default (cig-script#259's `auto`) gets a script onto the VM without the user asking and without a run that does the lowering itself:

| run of a script under the default | what runs it | what else happens |
|---|---|---|
| first | the tree-walker | an empty mark is left in the tin; nothing is started |
| second | the tree-walker | a `cig __lower` is left behind, which lowers the script and keeps its module |
| third and later | the VM | |

This is what each of those runs costs, on three scripts: `hello`, the smallest of [the benchmark programs](../bench/compute/hello.cig); [`bench/engines/lines-500.cig`](../bench/engines/lines-500.cig), 500 lines of small functions; and cigo's `orchestrate.cig`, 20,992 lines (cig-orchestrator at `e0c21a7`, run with no arguments, which prints its help). It was measured for [#254](https://github.com/otmof-ops/cig-script/issues/254) and [#259](https://github.com/otmof-ops/cig-script/issues/259), beside [the benchmark programs](ENGINES-2026-11-25.md), on the same machine with the same cig: commit `7e76bb8` (merged to `main` as `cebd9dd`, [#287](https://github.com/otmof-ops/cig-script/pull/287)), built as a release is.

Every measured number here is made from the samples in [`bench/results/2026-11-25-engines/`](../bench/results/2026-11-25-engines/) (`start/`, and where the text says so `start-one-cpu/`, `before/` and `before-one-cpu/`) by [`bench/compare/report.py`](../bench/compare/report.py), and made again by [`bench/compare/check.py`](../bench/compare/check.py).

## In short

- **A first run under the default is the tree-walker's.** `hello` takes {{median.hello.cig-auto-cold}} ms against the tree-walker's {{median.hello.cig-tree}}, {{ratio.hello.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} of the time ({{within10.hello.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}}); the 500-line script {{median.lines-500.cig-auto-cold}} ms against {{median.lines-500.cig-tree}}, {{ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} ({{within10.lines-500.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}}); cigo {{median.orchestrate.cig-auto-cold}} ms against {{median.orchestrate.cig-tree}}, {{ratio.orchestrate.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} ({{within10.orchestrate.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}}). With every process held to one CPU the three come to {{earlier:start-one-cpu:ratio.hello.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}}, {{earlier:start-one-cpu:ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} and {{earlier:start-one-cpu:ratio.orchestrate.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}}. #259's bar for making `auto` the default is a first run within 10% of the tree-walker's.
- **A second run starts the lowering, and pays for starting it.** The tree-walker runs the script again, and before `cig` returns it starts a `cig __lower`: `hello` takes {{median.hello.cig-auto-second}} ms, {{ratio.hello.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}} of the tree-walker's time; the 500-line script {{median.lines-500.cig-auto-second}} ms, {{ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}}; cigo {{median.orchestrate.cig-auto-second}} ms, {{ratio.orchestrate.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}}. That is with a CPU free for the process left behind. Held to one CPU, that process shares it with the run that started it, and the run's exit waits behind the lowering: {{earlier:start-one-cpu:ratio.hello.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}} for `hello`, {{earlier:start-one-cpu:ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}} for the 500-line script and {{earlier:start-one-cpu:ratio.orchestrate.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}} for cigo. A script pays it once for each text it has had under one build of cig; `auto_lower = off` turns the lowering off.
- **From the third run on, the default is on the VM.** It starts cigo in {{median.orchestrate.cig-auto}} ms where the tree-walker takes {{median.orchestrate.cig-tree}}: {{ratio.orchestrate.cig-auto.cig-tree}} of the time. The tree-walker parses and checks the whole script at every start; the VM loads the module it kept. The 500-line script takes {{median.lines-500.cig-auto}} ms against {{median.lines-500.cig-tree}}, {{ratio.lines-500.cig-auto.cig-tree}} of the time. On `hello` the engines take the same time, and its three medians (the tree-walker's {{median.hello.cig-tree}} ms, the VM's by name {{median.hello.cig-vm}}, the default's {{median.hello.cig-auto}}) differ by what copies of one run differ by here.
- **Asked for by name, the VM lowers a script inside its first run.** `cig run --engine vm` with nothing in the tin: {{median.hello.cig-vm-cold}} ms for `hello`, {{ratio.hello.cig-vm-cold.cig-tree}} times the tree-walker's; {{median.lines-500.cig-vm-cold}} ms for the 500-line script, {{ratio.lines-500.cig-vm-cold.cig-tree}} times; and {{median.orchestrate.cig-vm-cold}} ms for cigo, {{ratio.orchestrate.cig-vm-cold.cig-tree}} times. The default leaves that work to a process of its own, started once the script's own work is done.
- **Why the lowering waits for the second run.** The build before this one (`main` at `da5cd6f`) started it on a script's first run. Measured the same way, that first run took {{earlier:before:ratio.hello.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} of the tree-walker's time on `hello` and {{earlier:before:ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} on the 500-line script with a CPU free for the process left behind, and {{earlier:before-one-cpu:ratio.hello.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} and {{earlier:before-one-cpu:ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} held to one CPU. Starting a process costs a few tenths of a millisecond, which is little beside most runs and a good part of the smallest; and a script that is run once never gets it back. So a first run now only leaves a mark, and the process is started for a script that has come back.

